# Build context for packages/console/Dockerfile.
#
# Next to the Dockerfile rather than at the repository root, for the same reason
# packages/docs has its own: the root is not this package's to edit, and the
# build takes the repository root as its context because the console is one
# package of a pnpm workspace -- it needs its siblings to be present to build.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` would carry the host's installed dependencies and
# build output into the image, which both inflates it and risks a Linux build
# picking up a Darwin or Windows native binary the host happened to have.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.source
**/dist
**/.tanstack
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/coverage
**/*.log

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
